```java
// using PreparedStatement WRONG: value concatenated into the template
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '" + user + "'";
PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql);  // structure already poisoned
ps.executeQuery();  // injection still possible -> placeholder not used!
```

```java
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?";  // structure fixed
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ps.setString(1, user);   // value bound separately, as data
    ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery();
}
// DB compiled the query BEFORE seeing 'user', so input can't be SQL
```

*The placeholder must replace the value; never build the SQL string from input.*

```java
// ? cannot parameterize a column name, so validate against an allow-list
String sortCol = request.getParameter("sort");      // e.g. "name"
List<String> allowed = List.of("name", "created_at", "email");
if (!allowed.contains(sortCol)) throw new IllegalArgumentException("bad sort");

String sql = "SELECT id, name FROM users ORDER BY " + sortCol;  // safe: from allow-list
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery();
}
// values still use ? + setXxx; only validated identifiers are concatenated
```

```java
// concatenated JPQL — injectable
String jpql = "SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.email = '" + email + "'";
em.createQuery(jpql, User.class).getResultList();

// concatenated native SQL — also injectable
em.createNativeQuery("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '" + email + "'");
```

```java
// named parameter — safe
List<User> users = em.createQuery(
        "SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.email = :email", User.class)
    .setParameter("email", email)   // bound as data
    .getResultList();

// native query also supports binding:
em.createNativeQuery("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?1")
  .setParameter(1, email);
```

*Spring Data `@Query` and derived methods parameterize too — the rule is: bind, never concatenate.*

```sql
-- create a dedicated app account with minimal rights
CREATE USER app_user WITH PASSWORD 'secret';
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON orders, users TO app_user;
-- deliberately NOT granted: DROP, ALTER, DELETE on others, superuser

-- a separate read-only account for reporting:
CREATE USER report_user WITH PASSWORD 'secret';
GRANT SELECT ON sales_summary TO report_user;
```

*Even if an attacker injects, they can only perform actions these grants permit.*

